ame  according to Addison Rae when she first  joined up she had about 2.8 million  followers and now she's grown to 39  point seven million  Thomas claims people are always trying  to join hype house to promote their  content but its intention is to inspire  creators and promote collaborations not  just to give people their 15 minutes of  fame during an interview with Forbes in  February 2020 time aside he expects the  next generation of tick stalkers will  take over the house in the next five  years so while Charlie and Dixie leaving  may seem sudden to their fans it could  really be part of the team's long-term  plan the goal isn't to stay in Heights  house forever it's to take what you  learned there and apply it to your  future career there's also been  speculation that Addison Rae is either  leaving or has already left the hype  house although nothing is confirmed yet  she could be ready to move on just like  Charlie and Dixie if Thomas is right and  it's just a matter of time before  Addison and other existing members leave  and that isn't necessarily a bad thing  while hype house is losing some of the  current biggest tick tock stars don't  forget that even people like Charlie  once started out with just a few fans  instead of the hype house totally  collapsing after the loss of Charlie and  Dixie it will now have room for new  members to join be inspired and take  part in some amazing collaborations with  seasoned tik-tok stars do you think  Charlie and Dixie are leaving the hype  house so they can move on to the next  step of their careers or is there  something else going on share your  thoughts and theories with us and your  fellow fans in the comment section and  don't forget to click that subscribe  button for more videos from the things  bye for now

